1. THE CURRENTS BY CLASS (each from its pinned source)
   continuous: the pack's declared 10.0 A (pcb_pack_protection.yaml); the drafted states at the gauge's 10.0 V floor (record l9pwr
     section 6, Layer 8's copy): the largest sustained PLAN 9.63 A (PS-BUSY), at HIGH 14.97 A (PS-BUSY); with the outlets PLAN 19.20 A (PS-BUSY plus both outlets);
     above 10.0 A a sustained state is held by the shedding control (rv-pwr 9.3), so 10.0 A is the continuous design current
   transient: every transmitter keyed, 18.0 A for at most 60 s (PWR-F12, D-11's key-down ended early above 18.0 A); the largest
     key-down row at PLAN at 10.0 V 21.93 A (PS-ALLTX), held under 18.0 A by D-11's floors; the PA's key-on step 6.4 to 9.6 A at the pack
     (POWER-THERMAL 7.3); the docking pulse 242.9 A peak with a 33.8 us time constant, once per docking (L4-E11 E11-30), I2t 0.9971 A2s
   fault, the gauge working (PRIMARY-CONFIGURATION.md, the image): OCD1 20.0 A for 2 s; OCD2 24.0 A for 1 s; AOLD 30.0 A for 0.02 s; ASCD 55.6 A for 244 us
     so 20.0 A may be held without a trip (OCD1 never trips below it)
   fault, the gauge failed (the hardware backstop): the 25 A MINI blades in series (board P's F1, board E's F3, board A's F1;
     Littelfuse 297): 110 % (27.50 A) holds 360000 s at least; 135 % (33.75 A) opens in 0.75 to 600 s; 200 % (50.00 A) opens in 0.15 to 5 s; 350 % (87.50 A) opens in 0.08 to 0.5 s; 600 % (150.00 A) opens in 0.03 to 0.1 s
     typical I2t 625 A2s, cold 2.36 mOhm; F2 (Eaton SCF9550, board P) 30 A: 100 % for 1 h minimum, 200 % opens within 60 s, breaks 80 A
     prospective fault 240 to 480 A (pcb_energy_chain.yaml PACK_CELLS)
   the shore input: _VEH_T 6.15 A (the hot-swap's limit at VCL max) continuous; F1 10 A MINI: 110 % holds 360000 s; 135 % 0.75 to 600 s; 200 % 0.15 to 5 s; 350 % 0.08 to 0.5 s; 600 % 0.03 to 0.1 s
     (L4-E11 section 6); a stiff source to 900 A, 93 A2s typical melting, the clearing I2t not printed; L4-E11's D-06 selection:
     board E's copper from J_DCIN to F1 to the clamps at least 20 A continuous (a Layer 9 layout constraint)
   VIN_RAW: declared 14.10 A (the hot-swap and the tracker at the 9 V floor); the tracker's minimum buck valley limit 13.8 A

2. THE RULED METHOD AND THE CRITERIA
   rating: track_current.conservative (decision 35: the most conservative of the three Annex D fits at each area), outer copper
     at track_current.EXTERNAL_FACTOR 2.0, the rise bisected so the rating equals the current; widths by track_current.width_for_current
     at its 10 K default; the fits' stated data: IPC-2152 to 30 A and 100 K, CNES to 8 A (ECSS-Q-ST-70-12C D.2, D.3)
   adiabatic: Onderdonk's general form as records/l7pwr/inputs holds it, constants 234 and 33, copper melting 1083 C, from the
     consolidation's +70 C mixed-air line; a timed event's rise is the smaller of its adiabatic and its steady rise
   criteria (SESSION): the continuous load, the key-down, every gauge level and the blade's rating within the ruled 10 K (the rise
     every rating in the energy chain carries); the backstop's window and the hard short at or under 125 C from the air line, the
     blade's printed operating maximum (Littelfuse 297), the lowest printed limit of a part these bands join (the laminate's is NOT HELD);
     and every fault's I2t under the copper's own fusing I2t

3. THE SPLIT BETWEEN THE OUTER FACES (derived; copper's resistivity cancels)
   through-hole at both ends: equal faces sit at one potential along the band, so each carries half and stitching moves nothing
   a one-face part at one end: the part's face carries (Rb + Rv) / (2 Rb + Rv); at both ends (Rb + 2 Rv) / (2 Rb + 2 Rv), where Rb is
     one face's band and Rv the transfer field (one barrel over n). Stitching along such a band moves current onto the part's face early
     (that face sits lower all along), so the transfer barrels belong in a field at the part and nowhere between
   one barrel of 0.4 mm drill, 18 um plating: 65.08 (board A, 1.5384 mm) and 67.11 (board E, 1.5862 mm) in rho per mm, as much as 34.3 mm
     of a 14.60 mm 1 oz band
   with no field (one barrel), the part's face of a 14.60 mm band carries: 0.89 at 5 mm, 0.82 at 10 mm, 0.73 at 20 mm, 0.65 at 40 mm, 0.59 at 80 mm
   the field each one-face end needs for the part's face to carry at most 0.55 (one end / both ends), and the thermal count:
     pack, board A          14.60 mm, 1.5384 mm board: 5 mm 30 / 60, 10 mm 15 / 30, 20 mm 8 / 15, 40 mm 4 / 8, 80 mm 2 / 4; thermal 14 (via_current.barrels_for at half the coordination current)
     pack, board E          14.60 mm, 1.5862 mm board: 5 mm 31 / 62, 10 mm 16 / 31, 20 mm 8 / 16, 40 mm 4 / 8, 80 mm 2 / 4; thermal 14 (via_current.barrels_for at half the coordination current)
     shore 20 A, board E    9.70 mm, 1.5862 mm board: 5 mm 21 / 42, 10 mm 11 / 21, 20 mm 6 / 11, 40 mm 3 / 6, 80 mm 2 / 3; thermal 12 (via_current.barrels_for at half the coordination current)
     shore 10 A, board E    3.15 mm, 1.5862 mm board: 5 mm 7 / 14, 10 mm 4 / 7, 20 mm 2 / 4, 40 mm 1 / 2, 80 mm 1 / 1; thermal 6 (via_current.barrels_for at half the coordination current)
     VIN_RAW, board E       5.12 mm, 1.5862 mm board: 5 mm 11 / 22, 10 mm 6 / 11, 20 mm 3 / 6, 40 mm 2 / 3, 80 mm 1 / 2; thermal 8 (via_current.barrels_for at half the coordination current)
   on E7's placement CELL_F runs 5.65 mm from F3's pad to P_CP's land: 28 barrels at P_CP; the return 40.60 mm from J_BATT pin 1 to
