8. PREDICATES
   the quoted widths re-derive from decision 35's model: 6.72, 23.91, 11.95, 12.26 and 43.62 mm                           yes
   the blades on A, E and P are one rating and the chain's check 3 asks the conductor for it                              yes
   6.72 mm a face is over 10 K at the gauge's held OCD1 current                                                           yes
   6.72 mm a face is over 10 K at the blade's rating                                                                      yes
   11.95 mm on one 2 oz face is over 10 K at the blade's rating                                                           yes
   12.26 mm a face at an even split is at 10 K at the blade's rating                                                      yes
   the 14.60 class at its governing share is at 10 K at the blade's rating                                                yes
   on B1, B2 and B3 every load, transient and gauge level is within 10 K                                                  yes
   on B1, B2 and B3 the blade's 135 % held and its 600 s window top stay within the blade's printed maximum from the air line yes
   on A1 and A2 the blade's 600 s window top exceeds the blade's printed maximum                                          yes
   on every pack family the backstop's 5 s interval and faster are over the printed maximum by the tree's bounds          yes
   every hard short on B1, B2 and B3 is within the printed maximum at the blade's typical I2t and the gauge's ASCD        yes
   the copper is not the fuse: the 600 % row's bound on B1 and B2 is under the governing face's fusing I2t                yes
   with one barrel the part's face carries more than the governing share at every tabled length                           yes
   the transfer field's split count falls with length (one end and both ends)                                             yes
   the shore's 20 A families hold the fuse's 600 s window top at 10 K                                                     yes
   R17 reaches its rating inside the blade's 110 to 200 % window                                                          yes
   R19 reaches its rating inside the shore fuse's 135 to 200 % window                                                     yes
   the dock pins stay within their 10 C rating up to the blade's 135 % row                                                yes
   the XT60 is over its rating inside the blade's held band                                                               yes
   on board A two planes beside 12.26 mm faces are over the screen only in a band narrower than 30 mm                     yes
   a plane tied in parallel heats per square millimetre at the thickness ratio of the bands it relieves                   yes
   VIN_RAW's declared current covers the tracker's minimum valley limit                                                   yes
   every one-face hop's copper dissipates under a tenth of its series part per millimetre                                 yes
